  "notes": "{浮|う}かぶ means to float or to come to mind.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: Intransitive ({自動詞|じどうし})\n- Pair: {浮|う}かべる (transitive - to float something, to bring to mind)\n- Pattern: Xが{浮|う}かぶ\n\nASPECT:\n- {浮|う}かんでいる: Is floating / has come to mind (state)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {頭|あたま}に{浮|う}かぶ (to come to mind)\n- {考|かんが}えが{浮|う}かぶ (an idea occurs)\n- {思|おも}い{浮|う}かぶ (to recall, to come to mind)\n- {顔|かお}に{浮|う}かぶ (to appear on one's face)\n- {水|みず}に{浮|う}かぶ (to float on water)",
